    <LABELS><LABEL variant="solid"><ICON name="chart-bar" /> ANALYSIS</LABEL></LABELS>
    <H1>Regulatory Tailwinds Create $340B Addressable Market Expansion in Next 18 Months</H1>
    <H2>Policy Catalyst Framework</H2>
    <SMART-LAYOUT variant="solidBoxes" cellSize="15">
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4>IRA Manufacturing Credits</H4>
        <P><B>$67B</B> addressable through 2032, 30% tax credits for domestic production</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4>EU Carbon Border Mechanism</H4>
        <P><B>$89B</B> compliance market, covers cement, steel, aluminum, fertilizers</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4>Carbon Credit Standardization</H4>
        <P><B>$127B</B> voluntary market expansion, Article 6 implementation</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4>Grid Modernization Mandates</H4>
        <P><B>$57B</B> infrastructure investment, interconnection queue clearing</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
    </SMART-LAYOUT>
    <H2>Implementation Timeline and Market Unlocks</H2>
    <TABLE>
      <TR><TH>Quarter</TH><TH>Policy Implementation</TH><TH>Market Impact</TH></TR>
      <TR><TD><B>Q1 2025</B></TD><TD>EU CBAM full implementation</TD><TD>$23B immediate compliance spending</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD><B>Q2 2025</B></TD><TD>US Treasury 45V hydrogen guidance</TD><TD>$34B production credit clarity</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD><B>Q3 2025</B></TD><TD>Article 6 carbon markets operational</TD><TD>$45B international transfer mechanism</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD><B>Q4 2025</B></TD><TD>FERC Order 2023 grid reforms</TD><TD>$18B transmission investment acceleration</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD><B>Q1 2026</B></TD><TD>California LCFS expansion</TD><TD>$12B low-carbon fuel standard extension</TD></TR>
    </TABLE>
